# auto_config

Repository connected with CUS project

usage: generate_config.py [-h] [-i BTS_ID] -b BUILD -t TYPE [-p PROFILE]
                          [-l LOG_PATH] [-o OUTPUT_DIR] [-n1 RELEASE_N1]
                          [-v VLAN_ID] [-c CUSTOM_DIR] [-y YAML_MAP]

Auto config generator

optional arguments:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  -i BTS_ID, --bts_id BTS_ID
                        eg. enb1=1:enb2=2
  -b BUILD, --build BUILD
                        eg. SBTS21B_2104_001_0.0
  -t TYPE, --type TYPE  eg. FSM4
  -p PROFILE, --profile PROFILE
                        eg. CLOUD_R4A_CUS
  -l LOG_PATH, --log_path LOG_PATH
                        eg. /home/ute/testline_init_results/logs
  -o OUTPUT_DIR, --output_dir OUTPUT_DIR
                        Output directory with generated files
  -n1 RELEASE_N1, --release_n1 RELEASE_N1
                        Generate scfc file for release n-1
  -v VLAN_ID, --vlan_id VLAN_ID
                        Vlan_id for all enb's
  -c CUSTOM_DIR, --custom_dir CUSTOM_DIR
                        Path to directory with custom yaml profiles
  -y YAML_MAP, --yaml_map YAML_MAP
                        Specify yamls which needs to be substituted in profile
                        configuration, e.g. env=env.yaml

Example usage: 

generate_config.py --bts_id 1 --fsm_type=fsm4 --profile=CLOUD_R4BO9_3CUS_TDD --build=SBTS20C_2006_001_0.0 -o /home/ute/test

Testing:

You can test generated output by comparing it to reference files. Just run script located in AUTO_CONFIG_TEST/bin/
and if files are the same you will only see 'OK' output in every case.
